06,-1.1205610462639015e-05,-7.080780778778717e-05,-0.8023808598518372,-7.152555099310121e-07,-1.1920928244535389e-07,-0.010226943530142307,0.0,-1.0728830375228426e-06,0.0,0.0,-1.07287787614041e-05,0.0,0.0,-5.686121585313231e-05,0.0,0.0,0.0,-7.152555099310121e-07,-3.576272320060525e-06,0.0,-3.4570634852570947e-06,-2.9802276912960224e-06],"request":{"active_prefix":"","input_ids":[151644,8948,198,2610,525,1207,16948,11,3465,553,54364,14817,13,1446,525,264,10950,17847,13,151645,198,151644,872,198,50,3948,279,3491,3019,553,3019,13,20678,697,1590,4226,304,1124,79075,90,1112,92,382,10061,57960,10374,13233,90,64,2137,3,57960,10374,13233,90,65,2137,3,323,57960,10374,13233,90,66,31716,387,2326,4982,22879,11,1741,429,279,9210,1948,894,315,1105,374,279,29783,9210,57960,15976,2418,220,576,8123,315,279,27853,32507,291,2248,7907,553,1493,2326,22879,374,57960,37018,90,16,15170,59,26888,90,18,21,15,3417,2418,220,7379,198,78045,18,1124,9407,61,17,1124,15976,481,220,17,1124,9407,61,18,1124,15976,7110,60,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nLet $\\mathbf{a},$ $\\mathbf{b},$ and $\\mathbf{c}$ be three unit vectors, such that the angle between any of them is the acute angle $\\theta.$  The volume of the tetrahedron generated by these three vectors is $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{360}}.$  Find\n\\[3 \\cos^2 \\theta - 2 \\cos^3 \\theta.\\]","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"50a23365e77b7b315009d3f47fd85e1dc6a5cfe6a69ce0b811c9d95880bce246"},"seconds":49.24539279937744,"seed":733696185813744499,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve the problem, we will use the formula for the volume of a tetrahedron formed by three vectors \\(\\mathbf{a}, \\mathbf{b}, \\mathbf{c}\\), which is given by\n\n\\[\nV = \\frac{1}{6} \\left| \\mathbf{a} \\cdot (\\mathbf{b} \\times \\mathbf{c}) \\right|.\n\\]\n\nGiven that the volume \\(V = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{360}}\\), we can substitute this into the formula:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{360}} = \\frac{1}{6} \\left| \\mathbf{a} \\cdot (\\mathbf{b} \\times \\mathbf{c}) \\right|.\n\\]\n\nThis simplifies to\n\n\\[\n\\left| \\mathbf{a} \\cdot (\\mathbf{b} \\times \\mathbf{c}) \\right| = \\frac{6}{\\sqrt{360}} = \\frac{6}{6\\sqrt{10}} = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}.\n\\]\n\nSince \\(\\mathbf{a}, \\mathbf{b}, \\mathbf{c}\\) are unit vectors and the angle between any two of them is \\(\\theta\\), we can express the scalar triple product \\(\\mathbf{a} \\cdot (\\mathbf{b} \\times \\mathbf{c})\\) as the volume of the parallelepiped formed by these vectors, which is the determinant of the matrix whose columns are \\(\\mathbf{a}, \\mathbf{b}, \\mathbf{c}\\). This volume can also be written as\n\n\\[\n\\left| \\mathbf{a} \\cdot (\\mathbf{b} \\times \\mathbf{c}) \\right| = \\sqrt{1 - 2\\cos^2 \\theta + \\cos^2 2\\theta} = \\sqrt{1 - 3\\cos^2 \\theta + 2\\cos^3 \\theta}.\n\\]\n\nFrom the earlier result, we know\n\n\\[\n\\sqrt{1 - 3\\cos^2 \\theta + 2\\cos^3 \\theta} = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}.\n\\]\n\nSquaring both sides, we get\n\n\\[\n1 - 3\\cos^2 \\theta + 2\\cos^3 \\theta = \\frac{1}{10}.\n\\]\n\nRearranging the terms, we have\n\n\\[\n10 - 30\\cos^2 \\theta + 20\\cos^3 \\theta = 1,\n\\]\n\nor\n\n\\[\n20\\cos^3 \\theta - 30\\cos^2 \\theta + 9 = 0.\n\\]\n\nDividing the entire equation by 10, we get\n\n\\[\n2\\cos^3 \\theta - 3\\cos^2 \\theta + \\frac{9}{10} = 0.\n\\]\n\nThus, we need to find the value of \\(3\\cos^2 \\theta - 2\\cos^3 \\theta\\). From the equation \\(2\\cos^3 \\theta - 3\\cos^2 \\theta + \\frac{9}{10} = 0\\), we can solve for \\(3\\cos^2 \\theta - 2\\cos^3 \\theta\\):\n\n\\[\n3\\cos^2 \\theta - 2\\cos^3 \\theta = \\frac{9}{10}.\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the final answer is\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{9}{10}}.\n\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{\\frac{9}{10}}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
